BAR Droid phone version of BAR's draft pre-game UI (luaui/widgets/gui_pregameui_draft.lua, the pre-game when the game
sets a draft spawn order: start points chosen in turn; gui_pregameui.lua stands down then): its Ready / Lock button a
finger's height, as phone-widget-gui_pregameui.lua.patch makes BAR's other one. BAR sizes it by its interface scale,
40 high and words of 24 times it: about 48 pixels on the dev phone upright, 2.5 mm (2026-11-19, a skirmish started from
the lobby, the start point placed: this widget's button). At least 8.5 % of the screen's short side, its words as much
larger, and kept left of the screen's right edge; the spawn order's panel ("Team placement", from 78 % of the screen's
width, as wide as its names or the button) moved left until it ends on the screen, the button under it. Applied by the
engine (BarDroidPhoneLuaDir) to BAR's file as LuaUI loads it; if a block finds no place, BAR's own file runs.

@@@ find
	local currentButtonW = mathFloor(orgbuttonW * uiScale / 2) * 2
	local currentButtonH = mathFloor(orgbuttonH * uiScale / 2) * 2
@@@ with
	-- BAR Droid (phone): a finger's height, at least 8.5 % of the screen's short side
	local droidF = math.max(1, math.min(vsx, vsy) * 0.085 / math.max(1, orgbuttonH * uiScale))
	local currentButtonW = mathFloor(orgbuttonW * uiScale * droidF / 2) * 2
	local currentButtonH = mathFloor(orgbuttonH * uiScale * droidF / 2) * 2
@@@ end

@@@ find
			(buttonRect[2] + ((buttonRect[4] - buttonRect[2]) / 2)) - (buttonH * 0.16),
			24 * uiScale,
@@@ with
			(buttonRect[2] + ((buttonRect[4] - buttonRect[2]) / 2)) - (buttonH * 0.16),
			24 * uiScale * math.max(1, math.min(vsx, vsy) * 0.085 / math.max(1, orgbuttonH * uiScale)), -- BAR Droid (phone)
@@@ end

@@@ find
		buttonX = mathFloor(vsx * buttonPosX) + max_width / 2
@@@ with
		-- BAR Droid (phone): the team's placement panel on the screen whole (from 78 % of the width it ran past the right
		-- edge upright, and the button under it with it), the button under the panel as BAR has it
		x = math.max(0, math.min(x, vsx - max_width - 4))
		buttonX = mathFloor(x) + max_width / 2
		buttonX = math.min(buttonX, vsx - mathFloor(buttonW / 2) - (uiPadding or 0) - 2)
@@@ end
